      "writtenOn": "2024-01-02T21:09:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah good catch. I think it still works because by the time this function is called, `t.x` is clamped to be in `[0, 1]`. I believe the last valid offset in the array will have a value equal to `1` because we aren\u0027t using implicit starting and ending offsets.\n\nThe way the code is written isn\u0027t ideal, but when `t.x \u003d 1` we should be taking the `else` branch that mixes the last valid stop and the now-zero\u0027ed padding. The mix parameter will be `0 / -1` so should still be selecting the last valid stop (assuming that `mix(valid stop, half4(0), 0)`) does not somehow introduce error in the valid stop color value.\n\nWe could update shaders to use `\u003c\u003d` in the ifs so that we always mix up to the last valid stop, or I can go back to copying the last value. `memset` was easier here because of of the type change from a scalar array to two Vec4s. WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "a438e6f3_4320266a",
      "revId": "6d5d7e8b6a5eeb9c9cefc1342833aff48b7274e6",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
